diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -143,6 +143,13 @@

 ### crASHink patch updates

+- Added: tap saved highlights for on-page edge handles and a floating pencil/trash toolbar with rounded corners, a subtle shadow and round stem handles. The toolbar uses a shared action list and wraps automatically for future options. Dragging hides the toolbar; releasing saves the resized range while preserving text on other pages. Uncertain text mappings keep the full editor available without guessing a boundary.
+- Changed: hold briefly (200 ms) to start selection, then drag freely. Only release decides the action: one word opens the dictionary, multiple words save a highlight. Pausing while holding never opens a dictionary popup. Dictionary lookup also works on highlighted words.
+- Changed: saved clippings open directly in the full editor, with Save, Open, Delete and a top-right close button. Save is disabled when the selection matches the original, including after reversing changes.
+- Changed: successful highlights save silently without the Clipping saved toast or its pause; save errors remain visible.
+- Performance: touch drags coalesce to the latest finger endpoint, invert only words entering or leaving the range, and avoid full-page repaints for large selections. Saved-highlight resizing also reuses the current page, restoring only two small handle regions (512 bytes). Input and release are retained during panel refresh; page advance requires deliberate overshoot, and selection hit boxes stay inside actual words.
+- Performance: cache nearby words and queue word-control clicks during e-ink refreshes instead of rescanning the chapter for every click.
+
 - Changed: touchscreen page turns use swipes only; removed tap page-turn settings.

 - Keep every clipping reachable when TOC labels overlap: group by logical chapter and saved title, refresh on store changes, and freeze each rendered row window during navigation. Failed previews remain visible as selectable entries.
